Dedicated browser/display sidecar seccomp profile

The packaged desktop_chromium_seccomp.json derives from Moby's default seccomp
profile, licensed under Apache-2.0:
https://github.com/moby/profiles/blob/4b8214fc4971e06172938a1f1554ccff6647ee80/seccomp/default.json
Upstream file SHA256: 6416b47770785a41ac59073cdc77d9fe98517df2799dc83ef207e622de3053f6

Modification: prepend the clone/setns/unshare namespace allowance documented by
Microsoft Playwright (Apache-2.0), and a chroot syscall allowance required by
Chromium's user-namespace filesystem sandbox when all container capabilities
are dropped. All other Moby rules remain unchanged. These four allowances
have no argument filters. This modified profile is specific to the dedicated
display sidecar; it does not change the native AI workspace container policy.
https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/blob/91a765d1681cb3eeb0d0fb89fefec3cf0d21bd9b/utils/docker/seccomp_profile.json
https://playwright.dev/docs/docker
